>  <SOURCE_REFERENCES>
["https://doi.org/10.1002/wcms.1606","https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jctc.8b01176","https://doi.org/10.1021/om500230k","https://github.com/jensengroup/xyz2mol_tm/blob/db2734b084045ef895528c7a3d5040d38da23983/SMILES_csvs/csd_smiles.csv","https://github.com/jensengroup/xyz2mol_tm/blob/db2734b084045ef895528c7a3d5040d38da23983/SMILES_csvs/tmqmg_smiles.csv","https://github.com/uiocompcat/tmQM/tree/ece824419c9006fe66436daf233822b75533b82f/tmQM","https://github.com/uiocompcat/tmQMg/tree/e1dc9887b8f20a217a1db6ca972d726bcbaab45b","https://www.crystallography.net/cod/4083173.cif"]

>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Single-point calculation on the original coordinates and ligand-by-ligand Lewis review. The β-diketone fragment bearing two mesityl groups is monoanionic. The C₈H₈ eight-membered ring has two strong carbon–carbon multiple bonds and is drawn as neutral cyclooctadiyne. Adopt Ir(I). The reported cyclooctadiene and the input hydrogen count are distinguished in the record. Localized 12 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths. Use the supplied Lewis representation for scoring; Independent evidence for the complete graph is limited.

