>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Interactively reviewed graph. W–N–O 173.86°, N–O 1.20868 Å, g-xTB N–O WBO 1.4451. The closed-shell assignment for this near-linear terminal ligand is N≡[O+], with metal formal charge +0 and total charge +0. Terminal ligand identity, the remaining graph and charge balance were checked; The original M–N–O angle, M–N and N–O distances, and WBO agree with documented NO⁺ controls matched by metal, formal state, NO count and ligand class. Localized 15 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths. The atom order and coordinates of all 72 atoms agree between XYZ and SDF. Lengths of 71 nonmetal covalent bonds: 65 within range, 1 outside range and 5 with sparse controls. Examples outside range: 29–30 C-H 1.0939 Å. Use the supplied Lewis representation for scoring; Independent evidence for the complete graph is limited.

